# Klehomerie Technical Asset Management

> Independent, buyer-side Technical Asset Management in Athens, Greece. Klehomerie protects the physical asset behind the investment for international absentee investors, family offices, Golden Visa applicants, and the Athens expat community. Tagline: Don't just collect rent. Protect the concrete.

## Identity

- **Founder:** Arnaud Zerdab, former worksite manager (France)
- **Location:** Athens, Attica, Greece
- **Mandate:** Buyer-side only. Diagnostic, observational, protective.
- **Languages:** English, French, Greek

## What Klehomerie is not

Klehomerie is not a property manager, not an Airbnb co-host, not a handyman service, not a broker, and not a certified engineering practice. Findings are diagnostic and observational. Klehomerie does not issue civil engineering sign-offs, does not perform legal title work, and does not execute physical repairs. Where certification or legal sign-off is required, it is coordinated through licensed independent professionals.

Klehomerie operates a Master Asset Management System and Strategic Asset Management Plan structured with reference to ISO 55001. Klehomerie is not ISO 55001 certified.

## The four pillars

**The Gatekeeper, Red Flag Technical Scan (€97).** A 45-minute visual diagnostic producing a Go or No-Go verdict before capital is committed.

**The Authority, Golden Ticket Technical Audit (€490).** A 40-point audit across six fixed asset classes, with moisture mapping, root cause analysis, and a 5-Year CapEx forecast.

**The Guardian, continuous protective monitoring.**
- Asset Management Core (€140/month) and Premium (€190/month)
- Vacant Asset Guardianship Core (€120/month) and Premium (€180/month)

**The Coordinator, activation and execution oversight.**
- Asset Activation (€350): utility switch, key collection, Digital Vault creation, inventory check
- Technical Project Management (€65/hour)
- Technical Site Call-Out (€85), minimum charge including the first hour

All prices are exclusive of VAT. VAT 24% is charged in addition.

## The six asset classes

The Golden Ticket Technical Audit inspects a fixed six-part taxonomy, identical on every property so that reports remain comparable over time.

1. General Environment
2. Electrical Systems
3. Plumbing and HVAC
4. Joinery and Closings
5. Finishes and Surfaces
6. Amenities and White Goods

## The four-tier finding scale

Every inspected item is scored against the same four tiers on every visit and every property.

- **Critical Failure:** a safety, security, or structural risk requiring an owner decision now
- **Minor Defect:** no immediate danger, belongs in maintenance and CapEx planning
- **Conformed:** meets the expected standard, no action needed
- **Not Applicable:** not relevant to this asset

## CapEx discipline

Forecast accuracy is measured, not asserted. The 5-Year CapEx estimate produced during the Golden Ticket Technical Audit is compared against the actual contractor quotation when work is proposed. Once work is contracted, spend is tracked line by line against budget so scope creep is visible while it is still small.

## Emergency mobilization threshold

Below **€150**, Klehomerie may mobilize to stabilise an urgent situation without prior owner authorization. Above €150, explicit owner authorization is required before any funds are committed.

## Independence

- **Buyer-side only.** No commercial partnerships, referral agreements, or financial ties with Athens real estate agencies, brokers, sellers, or developers.
- **Zero commissions.** No kickbacks, finders' fees, or rebates from contractors, architects, or vendors. All compensation comes from the asset owner.
- **Advisory separated from execution.** Klehomerie never sells repair or construction services, which removes any incentive to overstate a defect.

## Vendor screening

Contractors entering the Klehomerie vendor pool must hold active GEMI registration, a minimum 4.8 average public rating, and a minimum of 15 years of documented activity, alongside a maintained internal rating and referral status.

